 ## 2026-09-11
 
+### 1730 — Doctor Now Names Every Missing Profile Field In One Run
+
+- ROOT CAUSE: BUG-260830-5pmaiz. `parsePiRuntimeSharing` and its sibling parsers (`parsePiProfile`, `parsePiRuntime`, `parsePiLifecycleLogRetention`) return on the first absent required field by design — correct for the fail-closed production launch path, but it meant `agents-infra doctor local` also stopped at field one, so diagnosing the 2026-08-30 incident (8 missing `runtime.sharing` fields) cost one invocation per field.
+- FIX: `tools/agents-infra/internal/infra/project_config_field_gaps.go` adds `projectPiProfileFieldGaps`/`missingPiProfileFields`, a read-only presence-only scan that re-parses each ancestor project config with a bare `toml.Unmarshal` (not the strict parser) and mirrors the required-field schema to collect every absent field at once, each tagged with dotted field path + config source path + a human-readable expected-value description. `Doctor()` (infra.go) populates `Report.PiProfileFieldGaps` from this scan regardless of whether the strict compose succeeds; `agents-infra doctor local` prints all of them.
+- DECISION: The scan is strictly additive next to the existing gate, not a replacement — `parsePiRuntimeSharing` et al. are byte-for-byte unchanged, so the production launch path keeps refusing on the first missing field with the same wording (verified via the full tools/agents-infra suite, including the pre-existing `TestParsePiRuntimeSharingIsStrictAndOptIn` wording assertions).
+- GATE: `TestDoctorReportsEveryMissingSharedRuntimeFieldInOneInvocation` (negative: strips all 8 late-added `runtime.sharing` fields from a valid profile, asserts `Doctor()` names all 8 plus config path in one call, and that `Doctor()` still refuses) and `TestDoctorReportsNoFieldGapsForValidSharedRuntimeProfile` (positive control: valid profile reports zero gaps). Narrowing mutant (drop the `resource_pressure_mode` presence check) kills the negative test; reverted after confirming.
+- SCOPE: agents-infra half only (`tools/agents-infra`). The task-board half — making a degraded/bare-launch spawn visibly prominent in spawn result/status/observe instead of one line among startup notes — is a separate ticket, BUG-260911-2tvq62, owned by skill-project-management; not touched here.
+
 ### 1345 — Environment Admission Has a Coincidental Second Gate
 - FINDING: `validateProjectTarget` (tools/agents-infra/internal/infra/project_config.go) now refuses an unadmitted `environment` value through `ValidateLaunchableEnvironment` (agents_management_registry.go, TASK-260911-39bag5), but a downstream vendor/environment pairing `switch`'s `default` arm ALSO refuses any pair it does not explicitly admit — with a different message (`"vendor/environment pair %s/%s is not admitted"` vs `"must be one of codex, claude-code, pi"`). A mutant that let an unadmitted environment (e.g. a registered-but-unlaunchable agentic system such as `gemini-cli`) past the first gate was still coincidentally caught by the second when driven with a made-up vendor/environment pair, so a test asserting only `err != nil` at that call site passed against the mutant for the wrong reason.
 - FIX: `TestValidateProjectTargetRefusesRegisteredButUnlaunchableEnvironmentAtTheRealCallSite` asserts the specific gate's own wording, not mere error presence, to prove which gate actually refused.
 - DECISION: agentic-system admission must always cross-check TWO things together — a program-local launchable-set declaration AND membership in `skill-agents-management`'s `pkg/agentic.Default` — never registry membership alone: `agentic.Default` is a wider global registry (also carries `gemini-cli`, `muse`, `qwen-code`, `antigravity` when those plugin packages are imported anywhere in the binary).
 - SCOPE: TASK-260911-39bag5 (STORY-260830-37bq03); `project_config.go`, `canonical_target.go`, `primary_session_launch_plan.go`, `agents_management_registry.go`.
 
+### 1631 — Readiness Test Flake Had A Third, Undocumented Race
+- ROOT CAUSE: BUG-260830-1rths2 named two races in `TestPiLaunchReadinessServiceUnavailableStillHonorsRuntimeBoundsAtProductionEntry` (a readiness-count side-effect file read, and two racing terminal conditions). Fixing both and stress-testing at 3x concurrency x15 iterations (45 runs) surfaced a third: `writePiPersistentUnavailableServer`'s fake runtime wrote its pidfile only after `import http.server, os, sys, threading, time` — under heavy host load that stdlib import occasionally took long enough that the production 1s readiness deadline fired and reaped the child before the pidfile write executed, failing `assertRecordedPIDsGone` with "no such file". Same shape as the documented races: a test reading a side-effect file the production path may not have written yet.
+- FIX: pi_test.go — reordered the fixture script to write the pidfile immediately after cheap `import os, sys`, deferring `http.server`/`threading` imports until after. Scoped to this one fixture; did not touch the shared `assertRecordedPIDsGone` helper (9 other call sites) or production code.
+- EVIDENCE: 145 total concurrent top-level runs post-fix (45 + 100, up to 5 concurrent processes), zero flakes. Production-side mutant (halved the `waitPiRuntimeReady` deadline in pi_launch_posix.go) is caught by the named subtest `times_out_while_runtime_remains_alive`; reverted after.
+- ANOMALY: same "side-effect file races production path" shape also hit `TestPinnedPiNoModelDirectRPCBashBypassesToolCallHookWhileStandaloneExcludesRPC` in a single *serial* full-suite run (no concurrency needed) — pre-existing, unrelated to this ticket's scope, likely worth its own bug ticket since the shape recurs.
